  "question": {
    "text": "The correct order of acidic strength :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{Cl}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{7}>\\mathrm{SO}_{2}>\\mathrm{P}_{4} \\mathrm{O}_{10}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{K}_{2} \\mathrm{O}>\\mathrm{CaO}>\\mathrm{MgO}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}>\\mathrm{N}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{5}>\\mathrm{SO}_{3}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{Na}_{2} \\mathrm{O}>\\mathrm{MgO}>\\mathrm{Al}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{3}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Acidic character of oxide $\\propto$ Non-metallic nature of element. Non-metallic character increases along the period. Hence order of acidic character is\r\n\r\n$\\mathrm{Cl}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{7}>\\mathrm{SO}_{2}>\\mathrm{P}_{4} \\mathrm{O}_{10}$"
  }
}